{
  "raw": {
    "https://clsbe.lisboa.ucp.pt/system/files/assets/files/faculty-position-marketing-2026_1.pdf": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Quantitative Marketing",
      "description": "Deadline: October 1st, 2026  Palma de Cima, 1649-023 Lisboa Tel. +351 217 270 250 www.clsbe.lisboa.ucp.pt FACULTY POSITION IN QUANTITATIVE MARKETING Católica Lisbon School of Business and Economics, Portugal Católica Lisbon School of Business and Economics (Católica-Lisbon SBE) invites applications for a full-time tenure- track Assistant Professor position in Quantitative Marketing, beginning in September 2027. We seek an outstanding scholar whose research and teaching will contribute to the next stage of the Marketing group's development and reinforce the School's position as one of Europe's leading research -oriented business schools. Applicants should have completed, or expect to complete, a PhD before the appointment date. A Strategic Opportunity The Marketing group at Católica-Lisbon SBE has established internationally recognized strengths in consumer behavior, branding, marketing communications, digital marketing, and consumer decision making. As marketing is being reshaped by advances in data, artificial intelligence, and digital techno logies, the School is making a strategic investment to expand its expertise in quantitative and technology-enabled marketing. The ideal candidate will play an important role in shaping this next phase of development. Beyond contributing to teaching, the new faculty member is expected to build an internationally visible research program and foster interdisciplinary collaboration across the School, particularly with colleagues in Operations & Data Science. Research Profile We welcome applications from candidates with proven research interests in one or more of the following areas: • Marketing Analytics and Customer Insights • Artificial Intelligence in Marketing • Marketing Technology (MarTech) • Customer Experience Analytics • Pricing and Revenue Management • Digital Platforms and Data-Driven Marketing We are interested in scholars addressing important marketing questions using rigorous empirical, econometric, computational, or machine -learning approaches. Outstanding candidates working in closely related areas of quantitative marketing are strongly encouraged to apply. What We Offer Católica-Lisbon SBE is a research-intensive institution that provides an environment designed to support ambitious scholarship. Faculty are expected to pursue research aimed at the leading journals in marketing and related disciplines. The School offers competitive compensation, substantial research support, funding for conferences and data acquisition, an active international seminar program, and teaching loads that allow substantial time for research. Faculty also benefit from extensive opportunities for collaboration across disciplines, a highly international academic community, and a collegial culture that values intellectual curiosity, research excellence, and innovation in teaching. Palma de Cima, 1649-023 Lisboa Tel. +351 217 270 250 www.clsbe.lisboa.ucp.pt Candidate Qualifications Applicants for the Assistant Professor position should demonstrate outstanding potential for publishing in top -tier journals. Candidates at more senior levels should have an established record of high -quality publications in top journals in marketing or a closely related field, excellence in teaching, and the ability to strengthen the research profile of the Marketing group. We seek scholars who combine substantive marketing insight with methodological rigor. Proven experience with analytical and computational tools (e.g., R, Python, SQL, Julia, Stata, or similar) is important. We particularly value candidates who actively contribute to a vibrant academic community through collaboration, intellectual engagement, and collegiality, and who are enthusiastic about participating in the day -to-day life of the department, including regular on-campus interaction with colleagues, doctoral students, and students. The Marketing Group The Marketing group consists of internationally trained faculty with publications in leading journals including the Journal of Marketing, Journal of Marketing Research, Journal of Consumer Research, Journal of Consumer Psychology, Marketing Science, and other premier outlets. The group combines a collaborative culture with ambitious research goals and is committed to developing internationally recognized scholarship while delivering outstanding teaching across undergraduate, master's, MBA, and executive education programs. This appointment reflects the group's long -term vision of broadening its expertise in quantitative and technology - enabled marketing while building on its established strengths in behavioral research. About Católica-Lisbon SBE CATÓLICA-LISBON is consistently ranked among Europe's leading business schools and holds the prestigious triple accreditation (AACSB, EQUIS and AMBA). The School's programs are taught entirely in English and attract students and faculty from around the wor ld. Faculty are affiliated with CUBE, one of Portugal's leading research centers in economics and management, providing an excellent platform for interdisciplinary research and international collaboration. Located in Lisbon, one of Europe's most vibrant ca pitals, Católica-Lisbon SBE offers an exceptional quality of life together with a dynamic international academic environment. Application Procedure Applications should include: • Cover letter • Curriculum vitae • Research statement • Teaching statement • Job market paper or representative publications • Three letters of recommendation (for junior candidates) Priority consideration will be given to applications received by October 1st. Applications will remain open until the position is filled. Initial interviews will be conducted online, followed by campus visits for shortlisted candidates. For further information, please contact the Faculty Recruitment Office and the Chair of the Search Committee. Applications should be submitted to the Faculty Recruitment Office (internationalrecruit.clsbe@ucp.pt). Any questions regarding the position may be directed to Prof. Daniel Fernandes (daniel.fernandes@ucp.pt). "
    },
    "https://clsbe.lisboa.ucp.pt/system/files/assets/files/position-2027-economics-position-at-clsbe-in-lisbon-new.pdf": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Macroeconomics",
      "description": "Deadline: November 23, 2026  ASSISTANT PROFESSOR POSITION IN MACROECONOMICS AT CATÓLICA- LISBON, PORTUGAL STARTING SEPTEMBER 2027 Católica-Lisbon School of Business & Economics invites applications for a n Assistant Professor position in Macroeconomics, to start , preferably, September 1 st, 2027. We are looking for applicants with strong research potential (or track record) of top publications in Macroeconomics and the ability to teach effectively . Candidates must be able to communicate clearly both orally and in writing. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Applications must be submitted by November 23, 2026. Católica Lisbon School of Business and Economics CATÓLICA-LISBON is a leading European business school committed to research production at the highest level and excellence in teaching. The school seeks to develop outstanding graduates for high-level careers and to offer business leaders a lifelong learning environment. We are one of the top 25 business schools in Europe according to the Financial Times rankings and have been Triple Crown accredited since 2008. Our programs are taught mostly in English to an increasingly international student body. About 75% of our students at the MSc level are non-Portuguese. In the area of Economics, we currently offer two bachelor programs, one full-time MSc in Economics, and a PhD Program, as well as several programs in Finance and Management. Research Environment CATÓLICA-LISBON provides a vibrant research environment. The core research faculty consists of a diverse group of more than 40 members, with doctorates from top North American (including MIT, Chicago, Rochester, Stanford, Princeton, and UCSD) and top European (including INSEAD, LBS, and Tilburg) programs. Faculty in Economics have recently published in journals such as Econometrica, American Economic Review, Journal of Political Economy, Journal of Economic Theory, Journal of Monetary Economics, Journal of Econometrics, Journal of International Economics, European Economic Review, Journal of Public Economics, Review of Economic Studie s, and Review of Economics and Statistics. In periodic assessments conducted by the Portuguese Science and Technology Foundation’s panels of international experts, the CATÓLICA -LISBON research unit has consistently received the highest grade of Excellent. Living in Lisbon Lisbon has recently been ranked the safest capital city in Europe. It is a thriving cultural hub with a vibrant restaurant scene, diverse artistic activities and sporting events, a public healthcare system, historic architecture, and great weather with about 250 sunny days per year. Position Requirements Applicants should have earned a PhD in Economics by the date of the appointment and must demonstrate the potential to publish in top economics journals. Salary is competitive, and funding for research -related activities, including travel to international conferences, is provided. In addition, f aculty are encouraged to apply for research funding from the Portuguese Science Foundation and from European funding agencies. Tenure-track faculty are expected to teach the equivalent of 3 courses per year, in English. Application Procedure Applicants should send via the JOE system a cover letter highlighting their ability to meet the position qualifications and highlighting relevant aspects for (a) research, (b) teaching interests, and (c) their specific interest in CATÓLICA -LISBON and Portu gal. This latter item is crucial for a potential successful follow-up on the application. In addition, they should send the job market paper, an updated CV, and at least three reference letters. The application deadline is November 23, 2026. We will interview applicants via Zoom in mid-December. Selected applicants will be invited for a campus visit in January after the ASSA meetings. For additional questions, please send an email to internationalrecruit@ucp.pt "
    },
    "https://clsbe.lisboa.ucp.pt/system/files/assets/files/position-2027-finance-position-at-clsbe-in-lisbon.pdf": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Finance",
      "description": "Deadline: November 15, 2026  ASSISTANT PROFESSOR (TENURE TRACK) IN FINANCE OR ACCOUNTING STARTING SEPTEMBER 2027 Católica Lisbon School of Business and Economics (CATÓLICA -LISBON: www.clsbe.lisboa.ucp.pt/ ) is seeking applications for an Assistant Professor position with tenure track in Finance or Accounting, starting in Fall 2027. We are looking for candidates with strong research potential or a track record of top -tier publications in Finance coupled with effective teaching skills. Applicants should have excellent communication skills, both oral and written. The position offers a competitive compensation package based on qualifications and experience. Application Deadline: November 15, 2026. About Católica Lisbon School of Business and Economics CATÓLICA-LISBON is a leading European business school committed to high -quality research output and excellence in teaching. The school seeks to develop outstanding graduates for high - level careers and to offer business leaders a lifelong learning environme nt. Our programs are internationally recognized. We rank among the top 25 business schools in Europe, with The Lisbon MBA and Master in Management programs listed among the top 20 in the Financial Times (FT) rankings. Our MSc in Finance is ranked 19th in the world. The international character of the school is reflected in our faculty, student body, and international accreditations. Since 2008, CLSBE has the “triple crown” of international business school accreditations (AACSB, EFMD, and AMBA). Our programs, taught entirely in English, cater to an international student body, with around 75% of our MSc students coming from outside Portugal. CATÓLICA -LISBON offers two bachelor programs in Economics and Finance, three full-time MSc programs in Finance, a part-time MSc in Finance, a PhD Program in Finance, and several executive education courses. In 2024, we established the Center for Sustainable Finance. Faculty CATÓLICA-LISBON provides a vibrant research environment. The core research faculty comprises about 50 tenure-track members with doctorates from top North American and European institutions. Our faculty represents numerous countries across the globe and includes a mix of both recently hired and established scholars. The CATÓLICA -LISBON research unit (CUBE) consistently earns the highest rating of “Excellent” from the Portuguese Science and Technology Foundation (FCT) and was recognized in 2019 as the leading research unit in Portugal for Management. The Finance and Accounting group includes 16 faculty members who regularly publish in leading journals. Living in Lisbon Lisbon is one of Europe’s safest capital cities. It offers a rich cultural scene, vibrant dining, diverse artistic activities, sporting events, excellent public transportation, a reliable public healthcare system, historic architecture, some of the best weather in Europe, and easy access to great beaches. Position Requirements Applicants should hold a PhD in Finance or a closely related field from a recognized institution by the time of appointment. Faculty are expected to maintain an active research agenda targeting top- tier journals. CATÓLICA -LISBON provides extensive research support and assists faculty in securing research funding from Portuguese and other European funding agencies. Candidates should be committed to engaging students in the classroom. Both tenure -track and tenured faculty typically teach up to three courses per year in English at the undergraduate, MSc, MBA, and/or PhD level, with the possibility of teaching in execut ive education programs. The teaching load may be reduced in the first year and concentrated within two of four teaching terms. With rare exceptions, all teaching takes place in the classroom. Part of the teaching load may be fulfilled by supervising MSc students writing their thesis. Candidates should be eager to contribute to the school's growth and its Finance programs and participate actively in the school's academic life. Regular on -campus availability, in -person teaching, and the ability to create and maintain collegial, harmoniou s working relationships with others are essential duties of faculty members at CATÓLICA-LISBON. Application Procedure Applicants should submit a cover letter that details their qualifications, highlighting their research and teaching interests. In addition, candidates should send their job market paper, an updated CV, and at least three letters of reference. The applicati on deadline is November 15, 2026. Initial interviews will be conducted via Zoom in early December. Selected candidates will be invited for an on-campus visit in January. Applications should be submitted via EconJobMarket. Please contact Eva Schliephake (cube.clsbe@ucp.pt) for questions regarding the position. "
    },
    "https://clsbe.lisboa.ucp.pt/system/files/assets/files/position-2027-operations-and-data-science-position-at-clsbe-in-lisbon_1.pdf": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Operations and Data Science",
      "description": "Deadline: October 31, 2026  FACULTY POSITION FOR THE OPERATIONS AND DATA SCIENCE RESEARCH GROUP STARTING SEPTEMBER 2027 Overview Católica-Lisbon School of Business and Economics invites applications for a full-time tenure track Assistant Professor position for the Operations and Data Science research group starting in September 2027. Experienced Assistant or Associate Professors interested in applying will also be considered in the search at their appropriate level. Applicants must have a PhD degree in a quantitative field such as operations management, operations research, decision sciences, information systems, computer science, statistics, or economics. The ideal candidate will have a robust research record, or show potential to produce research of the highest quality. Strong preference will be given to applicants with a demonstrated ability to leverage data science techniques in their research. Católica-Lisbon SBE is dedicated to developing high -quality, impactful research in connection with and application to industry to tackle business and economics problems. As such, successful candidates coming from programs outside business and economics are expected to develop research agendas that bridge to and can address managerial or economic problems. Priority consideration will be given to applications received by October 31, 2026, but applications will be accepted until the position is filled. The first round of interviews will be held online. Applications must be submitted via email to internationalrecruit.clsbe@ucp.pt Position Requirements Católica-Lisbon SBE is a research -focused institution and tenure -track faculty are expected to maintain a research program targeted at top -tier journals in their field. Católica -Lisbon SBE provides ample support to do so. Salary is competitive; the school provides funding for research- related activities, including travel to international conferences. Teaching requirements for tenure - track positions are reduced and scheduled with the goal of allowing ample research time. The school offers a collegial environ ment that encourages collaboration both among colleagues and with industry or institutional partners. Candidates must demonstrate the potential to publish in top -tier management journals. For Associate positions, candidates are expected to show a strong research track record in top journals, excellence in teaching, and the ability to add to the research re putation and productivity of the group. For all positions, a strong background in data science and the ability to integrate these techniques into research and teaching will be a key consideration. The faculty group of Operations and Data Science publish regularly in top journals such as Management Science, Manufacturing & Service Operations Management, Production and Operations Management, Operations Research, Information Systems Research, and Manag ement Information Systems Quarterly, among other top journals in the field. Católica Lisbon School of Business and Economics Católica-Lisbon SBE is a leading European business school, committed to research production at the highest level, to excellence in developing outstanding graduates for high -level careers, and to offering business leaders a lifelong learning environment. Ou r programs are internationally recognized: within Europe we are a top 30 business school, our Lisbon MBA and our Master in Management are top 25. The increasingly international character of the school is reflected in our faculty, student body, and international accreditations. Since 2008, Católica -Lisbon SBE has had the “triple crown” of international business school accredita tions: AACSB, EFMD, and AMBA. Our MSc, MBA, and PhD programs are entirely taught in English, to an increasingly international student body. Faculty and Research Environment Católica-Lisbon SBE provides a vibrant research environment. The core research faculty consists of more than 40 tenure-track members, with doctorates from top North American (including MIT, NYU, CMU, UCLA, Columbia, Yale, Arizona, Stanford) and top European (including LBS, LSE, UCL, Tilburg, RSM Erasmus, INSEAD) programs. The faculty body comes from all over the globe. The CUBE research unit of Católica-Lisbon SBE received the highest rating for research excellence in Portugal among all social science units , including business schools, when evaluated by an international panel. The Operations and Data Science research group at Católica -Lisbon SBE is composed of international faculty with a strong research focus. Living in Lisbon Lisbon has also been ranked as one of the top 3 cities in the world in terms of lifestyle. It is a thriving international hub with a vibrant cultural scene, diverse artistic activities and sporting events, fantastic restaurants, good public transportation, historic architecture, some of the best weather in Europe, a public healthcare system, and easy access to world-class beaches. Lisbon has recently been ranked the safest capital city in Europe. Application Procedure To receive full consideration, applicants must submit a cover letter, a CV, research and teaching statements, three letters of recommendation (for junior profiles), and a job market paper. Additional samples of written work are welcome but optional. Applications must be submitted via email to internationalrecruit.clsbe@ucp.pt - Priority consideration will be given to applications received by October 31, 2026, but applications will be accepted until the position is filled. "
    },
    "https://clsbe.lisboa.ucp.pt/system/files/assets/files/faculty-position-in-organizational-behavior-at-catolica.pdf": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Organizational Behavior",
      "description": "Deadline: August 20, 2026  Faculty Position in Organizational Behavior at CATÓLICA-LISBON, Portugal - Starting September 2027 Católica-Lisbon School of Business & Economics (CATÓLICA -LISBON: www.clsbe.lisboa.ucp.pt/) invites applications for a position in Organizational Behavior at the Assistant Professor level, to start September 1, 2027. Associate Professors interested in applying will also be considered in the search at their appropriate level . We are looking for applicants with strong potential or track record of high -level publications in Organizational Behavior. We are particularly, but not exclusively, interested in candidates doing research on micro OB topics such as negotiation, leadership, and emotions, as well as organizational learning and change . Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Applications should be submitted by August 20 , 202 6. In addition, we may interview candidates interested in the position during the Academy of Management 2026 conference by setting up an online call. For these preliminary interviews, please send us your (i) CV, (ii) job market paper , and (iii) a cover letter expressing your interest in the position by July 24, 2026. Católica Lisbon School of Business and Economics CATÓLICA-LISBON is a leading European business school, committed to research production at the highest level, to excellence in developing outstanding graduates for high-level careers, and to offering business leaders a lifelong learning environment. Our programs are internationally recognized: within Europe we are a top 30 business school, our Lisbon MBA and our Master in Management are top 25. In the world we are top 30 for our Masters in Finance and Executive education in the FT Rankings. The increasingly international character of the school is reflected in our faculty, student body, and international accreditations. Since 2008, CATÓLICA-LISBON has had the “triple crown” of international business school accreditations: AACSB, EFMD, and AMBA. Our programs are entirely taught in English to an increasingly international student body (75% international at the Masters level). Faculty and Research Environment CATÓLICA-LISBON provides a vibrant research environment. The core research faculty consists of close to 60 tenure-track members, with doctorates from top Nort h American (including Columbia, NYU, or Stanford ) and top Euro pean (including INSEAD, LBS, City University of London, Ecole Polytechnique, and Tilburg) programs. Associate and assistant professors include nationals of Belgium, Brazil, France, Germany, Greece, Italy, Portugal, Spain, and Turkey. More than 40% of our faculty are international. The CUBE research unit of CATÓLICA -LISBON has always received the highest rating for research excellence in Portugal since its creation in 1998 until 2026. It also received the highest evaluation for social science units in 2014, including business schools, as evaluated by an international panel. Faculty in management areas have published articles in Academy of Management Journal, Academy of Management Review, Management Science, Organization Science, Journal of Organizational Behavior, Human Relations, Journal of Business Ethics, and Strategic Management Journal among others, and have been members of the Editorial Boards of prominent journals, such as the Academy of Management Journal and the Journal of Management Studies. Living in Lisbon Lisbon has recently been ranked the safest capital city in Europe. It is a thriving cultural hub with a vibrant restaurant sc ene, diverse artistic activities and sporting events, good public transportation, a public healthcare system , historic architecture, among the best weather in Europe, and easy access to world-class beaches. Position Requirements Tenure-track faculty are expected to maintain a research program targeted at top -tier journals in their field (ABS 4* and 4). Católica-Lisbon provides them with ample support to do so. Salary is competitive, and funding for research-related activities, including travel to international conferences, is provided. In addition, faculty are supported to apply for research funding from the Portuguese Science Foundation (FCT) and other European funding agencies. Candidates should be motivated to engage students in the classroom. Tenure-track positions involve teaching the equivalent of 3 courses per year, in English, at the undergraduate, MSc and MBA levels, and potentially in executive education programs. Candidates must demonstrate the potential to publish in top -tier management journals (ABS 4* and 4) . For Associate positions, candidates are expected to show a strong research track record in top-tier management journals, excellence in teaching, and the ability to add to the research reputation and productivity of the group. All applicants should have earned a Ph.D. in a relevant discipline from a recognized school by the date of the appointment. Application Procedure In order to receive full consideration, applicants should send : (i) a cover letter, (ii) a CV, (iii) a one -page research statement, (iv) a one -page teaching philosophy, (v) three confidential reference letters, (vi) up to three samples of r esearch paper s, (vii) and teaching evaluations (if available) by August 20, 2026. We will host campus visits by invitation in the early Fall 2026. Applications should be sent by e-mail to: E-mail: internationalrecruit@ucp.pt Subject: OB Faculty Position_Candidate name Católica Lisbon School of Business and Economics Palma de Cima,1649-023 Lisboa Portugal "
    },
    "https://clsbe.lisboa.ucp.pt/system/files/assets/files/faculty-position-business-ethics-4.pdf": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Business Ethics",
      "description": "Deadline: May 22, 2026  FACULTY POSITION IN BUSINESS ETHICS AT CATÓLICA-LISBON, PORTUGAL Overview Católica Lisbon School of Business and Economics invites applications for a full -time tenure track Assistant Professor position for the Business Ethics group starting in September 2026. Experienced Assistant or Associate Professors interested in applying will also be considered in the search at their appropriate level. Applicants must have a PhD degree in a management field. The ideal candidate will present a robust research record, or show potential to produce research of the highest quality. Strong preference will be given to applicants with a demonstrated ability to deal with the normative and axiological issues of management in their research. Due to the school’s distinct doctrinal ethos, successful candidates must demonstrate a personal and professional commitment to the Christian principles and to the Catholic approach to society, companies and markets. CATÓLICA-LISBON is dedicated to developing high-quality, impactful research in connection with and application to industry to tackle business and economics problems . As such, successful candidates coming from programs outside business and economics are expected to develop research agendas that bridge to and can address managerial or economic problems. Priority consideration will be given to applications received by May 22nd, 2026, but applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Screening interviews will be held online. Position Requirements Católica-Lisbon is a research-focused institution and tenure-track faculty are expected to maintain a research program targeted at top -tier journals in their field. Católica -Lisbon provides ample support to do so. Salary is competitive ; the school provides funding for research-related activities, including travel to international conferences. Teaching requirements for tenure-track positions are reduced and scheduled with the goal of allowing ample research time. The school offers a collegial environment that encourages collaboration both among colleagues and with industry or institutional partners. Candidates should be motivated to engage students in the classroom. Tenure-track positions involve teaching the equivalent of 3 courses per year, in English, at the undergraduate, MSc and MBA levels, and potentially in executive education programs. The teaching load may be additionally reduced in the first year. Candidates must demonstrate the potential to publish in top -tier management journals. For Associate positions, candidates are expected to show a strong research track record in top journals, excellence in teaching, and the ability to add to the research reputation and productivity of the group. 2 For all positions, a strong background in data science and the ability to integrate these techniques into research and teaching will be a key consideration. Católica Lisbon School of Business and Economics (CATÓLICA-LISBON) CATÓLICA-LISBON is a leading European business school, committed to research production at the highest level, to excellence in developing outstanding graduates for high -level careers, and to offering business leaders a lifelong learning environment. Our programs are internationally recognized: within Europe we are a top 30 business school, our Lisbon MBA and our Master in Management are top 2 5. The increasingly international character of the school is reflected in our faculty, student body, and international accreditations. Since 2008, CLSBE has had the “triple crown” of international business school accreditations: AACSB, EFMD, and AMBA. Our MSc, MBA, and PhD programs are entirely taught in English, to an increasingly international student body. Faculty and Research Environment CATÓLICA-LISBON provides a vibrant research environment. The core research faculty consists of more than 40 tenure-track members, with doctorates from top North American (including MIT, NYU, CMU, UCLA, Columbia, Yale, Arizona, Stanford) and top European (including LBS, LSE, UCL, Tilburg, RSM Erasmus , INSEAD ) programs. The faculty body comes from all over the globe . The CUBE research unit of Católica -Lisbon received the highest rating for research excellence in Portugal among all social science units, including business schools, when evaluated by an international panel. The Business Ethics group at Católica-Lisbon is composed of international faculty with a strong research focus. Living in Lisbon Lisbon has also been ranked as one of the top 3 cities in the world in terms of lifestyle. It is a thriving international hub with a vibrant cultural scene, diverse artistic activities and sporting events, fantastic restaurants, good public transportation, historic architecture, some of the best weather in Europe, a public healthcare system, and easy access to world -class beaches. Lisbon has recently been ranked the safest capital city in Europe. Application Procedure To receive full consideration, applicants must submit a cover letter, a CV, research and teaching statements, three letters of recommendation (for junior profiles), and a job market paper. Additional samples of written work are welcome but optional. Your application should be submitted via e -mail to cube.clsbe@ucp.pt. Review of materials will begin immediately upon receipt. Priority consideration will be given to applications received by May 22nd, 2026, but applications will be accepted until the position is filled. "
    }
  },
